{
    "_doc": "The House: its tuning, family offices, Prestige sources and sinks, ambitions, and the demands made on a rich House (systems/house.js, systems/demands.js). systems/house.js keeps identical defaults for every table, used only when this data is not loaded; each table here is laid over them key by key. `config` is the Prestige/rival/role tuning; `roles` the five family offices (the member skill each scales off); `sources` the Prestige a notable deed earns (House.recordDeed) and `sourceScales` its multiplier by kind (a miracle, a festival's budget tier, an achievement's tier; 0 awards nothing); `sinks` the Prestige price of what gold cannot buy. An ambition's `requires` names the ambition that must be fulfilled first (its predecessor tier); `req` is a map of House._metrics keys to the minimum value (true for a flag). `reward` is paid when the capstone is reached: prestige, gold, renown, reputation (with every living realm), and an `honour` the House keeps forever — each honour's `fame` adds to the House's good fame in every realm (systems/fame.js).",
